WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.092 --> 00:00:17.956
Ben, Gaby and Mog returned to the garden, tired and feeling defeated.

2
00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:21.477
"Now what?"

3
00:00:21.977 --> 00:00:24.198
Ben panted, trying to catch his breath.

4
00:00:24.218 --> 00:00:27.679
"If we don't catch the gremlin, it's going to ruin the wedding!"

5
00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:32.265
"We could trap it, and then move it somewhere else," Mog suggested.

6
00:00:32.285 --> 00:00:34.346
"Like People Place!"

7
00:00:34.887 --> 00:00:36.287
the fish monster chimed in.

8
00:00:37.148 --> 00:00:38.049
Winnie frowned.

9
00:00:38.069 --> 00:00:39.410
"We can't do that.

10
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.572
This is the gremlin's habitat, and we're the Green Club, remember?"

11
00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:45.353
The others nodded.

12
00:00:45.373 --> 00:00:49.196
"I have a few ideas," Jen said.

13
00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:52.218
"I did some research while you were chasing the gremlin."

14
00:00:52.238 --> 00:00:53.899
"What did you learn?"

15
00:00:54.279 --> 00:00:55.040
Ben asked.

16
00:00:55.941 --> 00:00:57.301
Jen pulled out her phone.

17
00:00:57.321 --> 00:01:00.964
"'Garden gremlins keep their teeth sharp by gnawing on wood.

18
00:01:01.312 --> 00:01:02.932
They also love eating paper.'"

19
00:01:02.952 --> 00:01:05.293
"Aha!" Winnie said.

20
00:01:05.313 --> 00:01:08.734
"So that's what happened to Ben's map and the archway."

21
00:01:08.754 --> 00:01:17.356
"'Garden gremlins use camouflage to blend in with nature while they're collecting food,'" Jen continued.

22
00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.217
"'Their diet is varied.

23
00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:21.137
They eat leaves and flowers.

24
00:01:21.517 --> 00:01:22.658
Roses are a favorite.

25
00:01:23.238 --> 00:01:25.739
And they love monster food'!"

26
00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:29.980
"That explains the bruised blue roses and what happened to Mr.

27
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.044
Icky's food," Ben said.

28
00:01:32.064 --> 00:01:34.125
"What else does it say?"

29
00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:35.426
Gaby asked.

30
00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:43.469
"'Garden gremlins burrow underground, creating intricate tunnels, which sometimes can cause sinkholes to form.'

31
00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:47.451
Oh, and listen to this," Jen added excitedly.

32
00:01:47.471 --> 00:01:54.354
"'Garden gremlins will establish a home in a garden if their preferred habitat cannot be found.'"

33
00:01:54.374 --> 00:01:57.555
"And what's their preferred habitat?"

34
00:01:57.975 --> 00:01:58.815
Ben asked.

35
00:01:58.835 --> 00:02:01.441
"Mud!" Jen exclaimed.

36
00:02:01.961 --> 00:02:03.622
"Garden gremlins love mud.

37
00:02:04.042 --> 00:02:09.086
They use mud gardens to attract their mates, kind of like how birds use their colorful feathers.

38
00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:15.170
According to this article, a lonely garden gremlin causes a lot more trouble than one with a mate."

39
00:02:16.311 --> 00:02:17.451
Mog rolled his eyes.

40
00:02:17.471 --> 00:02:21.474
"Our gremlin must be really lonely then."

41
00:02:21.494 --> 00:02:23.455
"Poor fella."

42
00:02:25.577 --> 00:02:26.357
Winnie sighed.

43
00:02:26.377 --> 00:02:28.679
"What if we get him a mate?"

44
00:02:29.099 --> 00:02:30.060
Gaby suggested.

45
00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.221
"Then he won't cause any more trouble."

46
00:02:32.241 --> 00:02:34.063
"But how?"

47
00:02:34.463 --> 00:02:35.343
Waldo asked.

48
00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:38.846
"We can't just go to the pet store and buy a garden gremlin."

49
00:02:38.866 --> 00:02:41.848
"We can't," Winnie agreed.

50
00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:46.951
"But we can help him attract one by—" "Making a mud garden!"

51
00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:48.252
Mog exclaimed.

52
00:02:48.272 --> 00:02:50.754
"I've always wanted to make a mud garden!"

53
00:02:51.935 --> 00:02:52.915
Gaby laughed.

54
00:02:54.316 --> 00:02:56.278
"It looks like now is your chance, Mog."

55
00:02:56.298 --> 00:02:59.400
"Do you think this is going to work?"

56
00:02:59.828 --> 00:03:00.588
Jen asked.

57
00:03:01.609 --> 00:03:04.109
"There's only one way to find out," Ben replied.

58
00:03:04.129 --> 00:03:06.610
"Come on, everyone, we've got more work to do!"

59
00:03:15.412 --> 00:03:18.433
Ben adjusted his tie before taking his mother's arm.

60
00:03:22.314 --> 00:03:27.336
and your friends did great work," Mom whispered to Ben as they began to drift down the wedding

61
00:03:27.476 --> 00:03:28.796
aisle. "Thanks, Mom!

62
00:03:29.272 --> 00:03:30.712
Looks like the mud garden worked.

63
00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:32.913
We haven't seen the gremlin in days."

64
00:03:33.993 --> 00:03:38.515
Ben escorted his mother to a seat in the front row and then slipped into his own seat

65
00:03:38.595 --> 00:03:39.355
next to Winnie.

66
00:03:39.955 --> 00:03:42.036
The musicians had just begun to play.

67
00:03:42.056 --> 00:03:46.557
"The garden looks amazing," Winnie said.

68
00:03:46.577 --> 00:03:52.058
"Especially the roses on the archway, and the vines make the perfect backdrop."

69
00:03:53.039 --> 00:03:53.859
Ben grinned.

70
00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:55.879
"It all worked out.

71
00:03:56.099 --> 00:03:57.620
Thanks to you and the Green Club!"

72
00:03:58.636 --> 00:04:01.720
"Shh!" A wedding guest sitting behind Ben hissed.

73
00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.962
"Here comes the bride!"

74
00:04:17.117 --> 00:04:18.218
By now Mrs.

75
00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.880
Hubbletree was singing an aria.

76
00:04:23.368 --> 00:04:29.550
Ben and Winnie turned around to watch as Victoria, in a flowing gown made of spiderwebs and sparkles,

77
00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.070
walked down the aisle.

78
00:04:35.951 --> 00:04:41.493
Guests cheered as the glamorous bride joined a beaming Uncle Bert at the archway.

79
00:04:42.873 --> 00:04:43.373
When Mrs.

80
00:04:43.413 --> 00:04:46.874
Hubbletree finished the aria, Mayor Hubbletree cleared his throat.

81
00:04:50.595 --> 00:04:58.824
beloved," the Mayor began, "uh I mean deathly beloved, we are gathered here to join this ghost and

82
00:04:58.884 --> 00:05:09.351
this vampire in wedded bliss Later at the reception, Ben and Winnie stood watching Uncle Bert and Victoria

83
00:05:09.491 --> 00:05:10.892
start their first dance.

84
00:05:10.912 --> 00:05:17.477
"It was so nice of Bert and Victoria to invite the whole Green Club to their wedding," Winnie

85
00:05:17.557 --> 00:05:19.619
said. "Was it your idea?"

86
00:05:20.599 --> 00:05:21.340
Ben nodded.

87
00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.822
"It was the perfect way to thank everyone for their hard work."

88
00:05:32.729 --> 00:05:34.470
Winnie giggled, watching Mr.

89
00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.792
Freaky talk to a Hollyweird reporter.

90
00:05:36.812 --> 00:05:39.234
"I've never seen Mr.

91
00:05:39.314 --> 00:05:40.976
Freaky look so happy!"

92
00:05:40.996 --> 00:05:45.259
"Mrs. Hubbletree looks pretty happy too," Ben said.

93
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.720
Winnie grinned.

94
00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:51.952
"She hasn't left Tom Ooze's side since—" "Boo!"

95
00:05:52.593 --> 00:05:53.493
someone shouted.

96
00:05:53.513 --> 00:05:55.454
"Ahh!" Winnie jumped.

97
00:05:55.474 --> 00:05:56.875
"Did I scare you?"

98
00:05:57.495 --> 00:05:58.936
Sid appeared from behind her.

99
00:05:58.956 --> 00:05:59.797
"Did I?

100
00:06:00.057 --> 00:06:00.497
Did I?"

101
00:06:00.517 --> 00:06:02.278
"You sure did!"

102
00:06:03.979 --> 00:06:04.779
Winnie laughed.

103
00:06:04.799 --> 00:06:07.121
"That's the third time, Sid.

104
00:06:07.461 --> 00:06:10.082
You're definitely ready for your scare test!"

105
00:06:10.923 --> 00:06:12.904
Just then Gaby hurried over.

106
00:06:12.924 --> 00:06:15.485
"Hey, you have to see this!"

107
00:06:17.146 --> 00:06:20.908
She led them to the mud garden, where the rest of the Green Club was waiting.

108
00:06:21.388 --> 00:06:24.210
Then she pointed to something frolicking in the mud.

109
00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:27.813
"Look!" "Is that the garden gremlin?"

110
00:06:28.113 --> 00:06:28.833
Ben asked.

111
00:06:28.853 --> 00:06:33.296
"Nope." Jen sighed happily.

112
00:06:33.316 --> 00:06:36.259
"It's two garden gremlins!

113
00:06:36.619 --> 00:06:37.980
He found a mate!"

114
00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.362
"This is like a double wedding!"

115
00:06:41.802 --> 00:06:42.483
Mog said.

116
00:06:45.485 --> 00:06:49.228
Ben laughed, watching the garden gremlins roll in the mud.

117
00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:55.427
The two new partners looked happy—almost as happy as Uncle Bert and Aunt Victoria!
